
3. Performance Tuning (your 30% cost reduction claim)

⚠️ This is the bullet most likely to get deep follow-up questions. Have a specific before/after story ready — interviewers can tell the difference between a memorized list and a real experience.

Q: What specific techniques did you use to achieve the 30% cluster cost reduction?

Structure your answer as: Problem → Diagnosis → Actions → Result

"We noticed our nightly batch jobs were running longer than expected and consuming more DBUs than budgeted. I used the Spark UI / Query Profile to diagnose:

Data skew in a few large joins — one partition key (e.g., a specific product category or region) had disproportionately more rows, causing a few tasks to run 5-10x longer than others while the rest of the cluster sat idle. I applied salting on the skewed join key to spread that data across more partitions.
Excessive small files in Silver tables from frequent micro-batch writes — ran OPTIMIZE with ZORDER on frequently filtered columns, and set up a scheduled compaction job, which reduced file count and improved read performance for downstream Gold aggregations.
Over-provisioned clusters — several jobs were using fixed-size clusters sized for peak load year-round. Switched to autoscaling clusters and tuned min/max worker counts based on actual historical job profiles.
Enabled Photon engine where applicable for CPU-bound aggregation-heavy jobs.
Reviewed and removed unnecessary .cache()/.persist() calls that were holding memory without reuse benefit.


