How do you handle communication with the client?

What happened: The client once asked us to make the provisioning dashboard update "as close to real-time as possible," because they wanted to react quickly to problems.

How I responded: Instead of just agreeing right away, I explained to them what "real-time" actually means from a technical side — it means keeping servers running all the time, which costs more money and needs more monitoring from our team. I asked them what they were really trying to solve, instead of just building what was literally asked.

What we found out and did instead: After discussing, it turned out they didn't need updates every second — what they really wanted was to know quickly if an order was stuck somewhere for too long without progress. So instead of building expensive real-time streaming, we set the dashboard to refresh every 15 minutes, and separately added an alert that specifically flags orders that have been stuck for too long. This solved their actual problem in a simpler and cheaper way, and they were happy with this solution.
